11.0.0, fifth TestFlight upload — the app records the plugin purchase for the Audio Units

Since this build the app and the extension request the App Group group.com.echoelmusic.shared:
the app checks the purchase at launch and stores the answer there, and the Audio Units read it
before they ask StoreKit themselves (factory job 002). This archive also settles the open half of
F17: if the .auv3 profile does not grant the group, signing fails here and the run prints every
profile's groups — or it signs and AUM reports -3000, which is why the baseline comes first below.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10007), fourth upload — finding no earlier songs no longer marks the import
done (key studio.importedEarlierSongs.v2). Before that: 10006 (no tested host claimed), 10005
(About page), 10004 (the first Echoel Studio build). Those four carry no App Group entitlement.
group.com.echoelmusic (the import of earlier songs) is still not requested (F17).

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

What to try on the device (nothing here is device-verified yet):
- FIRST, the plugin purchase, in this order (FOUNDER_INBOX §2, family SP):
  1. Install 10007 again and load Echoel Synth, Drums and EQ in AUM — the baseline.
  2. Install this build and load the same three: no -3000.
  3. Without a purchase Echoel Synth still pauses after 28 s, every 30 s.
  4. Once the product exists in App Store Connect (F-15/E37): buy with the sandbox account in the
     app, reload Synth in AUM — no demo pause.
  5. As a buyer, sign out of the App Store, launch Echoel once, load Synth in AUM: say whether
     the demo pause comes back.
- Song menu → About Echoel: the page names the build, says what is in it and what is not,
  and its two links open in the browser. "Your data" names the App Store (at launch, and when
  you open the store: prices, buying, Restore Purchases) and Network MIDI (when you turn it on).
- Song menu → Echoel Plugins: the footer says the instruments are not yet tested in a host
  app on a device and not on sale yet. With no in-app purchase in App Store Connect (F-15/E37)
  the store says "The instruments are not on sale yet." and shows no price.
- In a host, an Echoel instrument that is not unlocked says the unlock is not on sale yet.
- Launch, make an instrument track, play notes from a MIDI keyboard; write notes in a part
  and drum steps on a drum track.
- Automate a synth parameter: notes still end and release.
- Record a take on an audio track; Stop fades it out, its reverb rings.
- Export a song with a long reverb: the file ends after the tail, not 2 s after the last note.
- Send the app to the background while stopped: audio stops; come back and play.
- Take a call while playing: the song does not resume by itself.
- Open Echoel Synth, Drums and Sampler in AUM or GarageBand: each loads and plays as a demo
  (two seconds of silence every thirty); the effects are free. Note host and sample rate.
- Open an older host session that used the earlier instrument: it now shows as
  "Echoel Synth (earlier sessions)" and still opens.
